de something or are trying to steal. Even if they're bluffing, they almost certainly have better high cards than my 7-5. Calling 160 chips with essentially no equity is burning money. With 8 more hands to play and currently down in the match, I should preserve my chips for better spots rather than call with one of the worst possible holdings.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
